course: dictionary
lesson: 11845
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is meant by looking at the words around it. The word blooming is a good example. «The roses are blooming along the garden wall» is about flowers opening, because roses bloom.
explain: «She looked blooming after her holiday by the sea.» Here blooming means healthy, happy and full of life, not flowers. The clues are looked and after her holiday. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Blooming can also be a mild word for annoyance or for emphasis. «That blooming dog has dug up the lawn again!» The writer is not talking about flowers or health. The word shows the speaker is cross, in a gentle way.
explain: The best check is to try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense. If more than one fits, read the whole text again to find more clues.
fact: Blooming comes from the verb bloom, so its -ing form is blooming.
fact: «Blooming» can mean having flowers that are open, or flowering: «The apple trees are blooming in April.»
fact: «Blooming» can mean healthy, happy and full of life: «The little girl looked blooming after her holiday.»
fact: In UK informal speech, «blooming» is a mild word used for annoyance or emphasis, as in «it's blooming freezing».
fact: «Blooming» can also mean growing and doing well, as in «a blooming business» or «a blooming friendship».
exercise: «The roses are blooming along the garden wall.» What does blooming mean here? | *Having flowers that are open | Very angry and shouting | Lost in the garden | Freezing cold
exercise: «She looked blooming after her long holiday by the sea.» What does blooming mean? | *Healthy, happy and full of life | Tired and cross | Dark and cloudy | Covered in mud
exercise: «It's blooming freezing in here, so put the heating on!» What does blooming show in this sentence? | A sign that the room is empty | A new kind of heater | *A mild, informal word for emphasis, like a gentle swear word | A flower that is opening
test: «That blooming dog has dug up the lawn again!» What does blooming show? | *Annoyance, in a mild way | Happiness about the lawn | The dog is sleepy | Flowers growing on the lawn
test: «The little shop is a blooming business now, with customers every day.» What does blooming mean here? | Cold and wet | Closed for the day | *Growing and doing well | Having flowers
exam: Read this: «Ella came back from camp looking blooming.» What does blooming mean? | Covered in mud | *Healthy, happy and full of life | Lost in the woods | Having flowers that are open
